Fixed: DoFAccessor::dof_index() and DoFAccessor::vertex_dof_index()
returned the degree of freedom of a different object, or accessed memory out
of bounds, when called on an object that is only adjacent to artificial
cells. With hp capabilities, they triggered an assertion instead. The same
applied to DoFAccessor::get_dof_indices() for vertices in 1d. These
functions now return numbers::invalid_dof_index for such objects.
DoFAccessor::get_dof_indices() on a face or line of an artificial cell moved
degrees of freedom to the wrong position if only some of them were stored.
It now returns numbers::invalid_dof_index for all of them.
